If we do not believe we can help them get promoted, we say so on the first call. They do not pay for that filter.\
Credibility (approved)\uc0\u8232 \'a0Mudit: former global CXO, 30+ years, 5 countries, ICF-PCC, TEDx, trained by John Mattone, 10,000+ leaders coached.\
Mentee companies: Google, Barclays, Shell, JP Morgan, Citi, Reliance (also Accenture, PepsiCo, Dell on his About).\
Named public testimonials: Gautam Bhat (Senior PM, Capgemini); Sachin Badole (Senior Director of Engineering, Tenstorrent); Deepa K C (Head of Infrastructure and Security, Vodafone); Mahesh Ranganatha (SAP S/4HANA, Schneider). Checkable on LinkedIn. Company-name anchors are fine (\'93leaders at Accenture\'94).\
What we can credibly talk about\uc0\u8232 \'a0The stall after Senior Manager / Director. Why delivery stops being the differentiator. Legibility in the promotion room. GCC: the India operator vs the person global can explain. The four pillars. The consult as a filter. Mudit\'92s operator background. The four named testimonials and those company names. Nothing we cannot source.\
